Q: How to render a multi-line text string in React A: <p>you need to add these 3 things,</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>maxWidth</strong>: '250px', with your required space to be occupied in width</li>
<li><strong>whiteSpace</strong>: '<strong>pre-line</strong>', and</li>
<li><strong>\n</strong> on your tooltip description message to show new line.</li>
</ol>
<pre><code>                      &lt;Tooltip
                        ref={refs.setFloating}
                        style={{
                          left: x,
                          position: strategy,
                          top: y,
                          maxWidth: '250px',
                          whiteSpace: 'pre-line',
                          color: '#F54927',
                        }}
                        {...getFloatingProps()}
                      &gt;
                        {'Your tooltip message to be added line 1.\nYour tooltip message to be added line 2.'}
                      &lt;/Tooltip&gt;
</code></pre>

Q: AIoT device: Radius Authentication using PHP with Message-Authenticator attribute A: <pre><code>The Message-Authenticator attribute (type 80) in RADIUS is not natively supported
by the PHP radius extension. It requires calculating an HMAC-MD5 hash of the packet,
which is typically handled by third-party PHP RADIUS libraries.

You can use a pure PHP RADIUS client library to do this, try
https://github.com/BlockBox2000/php-radius. It can be used for Iot, AIoT, or AI
applications, and file size is 32k only.

The one you need is b2radius.inc, and you can modify it.

    &lt;?php
    require_once('b2radius.inc');
    $radius = new Radius('192.168.11.1', 'testing123');
    if ($radius-&gt;AccessRequest('userid', 'userpw')) {
      echo &quot;Authentication accepted.\n&quot;;
    } else {
      echo &quot;Authentication rejected.\n&quot;;
    }
    echo $radius-&gt;GetReadableReceivedAttributes();
    ?&gt;
</code></pre>
